-- title:
--   Universal property of the level-ℓ Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation family
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the full Čerednik–Drinfeld frame for fake elliptic curves, to which a single prime $\ell$ of the Hecke tower and a scheme $M_\ell$ carrying a uniformisation family are adjoined; the conclusion is the universal property of that family in the category of functors on $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebras.
--
--   **Arithmetic frame.** Two distinct primes $r \neq \bar r$ and a nonzero level $N$ with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree. A coefficient ring $\mathcal O$: a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with an irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A further $\mathcal O$-algebra $Onr$, a characteristic-zero domain, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod \pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $v\!\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $v\!\det(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion algebra and moduli frame.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies over $r$ or over $\bar r$; a submodule $\Lambda$ which is an order maximal among orders (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a point assignment $pt$ sending each commutative ring $S$, each structure morphism $s$ and each fake elliptic curve for $(\Lambda,N)$ over $S$ to a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} S \to \mathcal X$ over $s$, such that `h𝒳` holds: the five clauses of `IsCoarseModuli` (invariance under isomorphism of fake elliptic curves, compatibility with base change along ring maps, surjectivity and injectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property among such assignments). The generic fibre, i.e. the pullback of $f$ along $\operatorname{Spec} K_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, is geometrically reduced and geometrically connected.
--
--   **Auxiliary full level and twisting group.** An integer $n \geq 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $n$ coprime to $N$; a scheme $M$ with $f_M : M \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and an assignment $ptF$ on fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure satisfying the four clauses of `IsFineModuli` (isomorphism invariance, base-change compatibility, and bijectivity of $ptF$ on $S$-points for every $S$). A group $G$, a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ and a labelling $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ with `hρ` : `IsLevelTwistAction` (the automorphisms lie over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, $\rho(g)$ implements the twist of full level structures by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n\Lambda$). A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), compatible with the point assignments in the sense that $ptF(u)$ followed by $p$ is $pt(u_1)$ (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke tower, degeneracies, Atkin–Lehner maps.** For each prime $\ell$ different from $r$ and $\bar r$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and an assignment $ptT_\ell$ on fake elliptic curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure satisfying the five clauses of `IsCoarseModuliT`; two degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell) : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) with $ptT_\ell(u)$ followed by $d_0(\ell)$ equal to $pt$ of the underlying curve (`hd₀`), and $ptT_\ell(u)$ followed by $d_1(\ell)$ equal to $pt(d)$ whenever $d$ is an $\ell$-isogenous quotient of $u$ in the sense of `IsLevelIsogeny` (`hd₁`). Two morphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ realising, on points, the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion data.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ ramified exactly at $\bar r$ among the finite places; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$; an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`), such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$; a height-one prime $v$ containing $r$.
--
--   **Discrete group data.** A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ equal, elementwise, to the group of units lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at all places other than $v$ (`hΓt`). Elements $s(\ell) \in \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and adelic units $sf(\ell)$ for each tower prime $\ell$ subject to `hs`: away from $r$ the component of $sf(\ell)$ is $s(\ell) \otimes 1$; at the places over $r$ it is $1$; the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the set `levelHeckeUSet` for $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$, and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise; and the reduced norm of $s(\ell)$ equals $\ell$. Subgroups $\Gamma_t(\ell) = \Gamma_t \cap s(\ell)\Gamma_t s(\ell)^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`). A homomorphism $\theta_t : \Gamma_t \to G$.
--
--   **Uniformisation families.** Write $\mathcal F$ for the functor on $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebras whose value at $B$ is $\bigl(\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O\text{-alg}}(Onr,B) \times \Omega(B)\bigr) \times G$, where $\Omega(B) =$ `Omega K₀ π` is the set of Deligne data over $B$ (for every full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M \subset K_0^2$ a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes M$ with invertible quotient, monotone in $M$, equivariant for homothety, and nondegenerate at each prime of $B$), and for $h : X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ write $X(B)$ for `Scheme.nilpPoints h` at $B$, the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} B \to X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. The data include $\Theta_f : \mathcal F(B) \to M(B)$ for every $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, and for each tower prime $\ell$ a family $\Theta_T(\ell)$ from $\operatorname{Hom}(Onr,B) \times \Omega(B)$ to $\mathcal Y_\ell(B)$, on which no further condition is imposed. The family $\Theta_f$ satisfies: `hnat`, naturality in $B$; `hG`, $\Theta_f(x, gh)$ followed by $\rho(h)$ equals $\Theta_f(x,g)$; `hinv`, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ and $x, x'$ related by `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\iota_0(\gamma)$ — that is, the $Onr$-component of $x'$ is the $\mathrm{Fr}^{-v\det \iota_0(\gamma)}$-twist of that of $x$, and the Deligne datum of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ — one has $\Theta_f(x', \theta_t(\gamma)g) = \Theta_f(x,g)$; and `het`, formal étaleness: for a surjection $p : B \to B_0$ of $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebras whose kernel has zero multiplication, every $y \in M(B)$ lifting $\Theta_f(x_0)$ comes from a unique $x \in \mathcal F(B)$ with $\mathcal F(p)(x) = x_0$ and $\Theta_f(x) = y$.
--
--   **Level-$\ell$ data.** A tower prime $\ell$, a scheme $M_\ell$ with $f_{M_\ell} : M_\ell \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ which is locally of finite type (`hfMℓ`), and a family $\Theta_{f,\ell} : \mathcal F(B) \to M_\ell(B)$ for every $\pi$-nilpotent $B$, subject to: `hnatℓ`, naturality in $B$; `hinvℓ`, the twisted invariance $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x',\theta_t(\gamma)g) = \Theta_{f,\ell}(x,g)$ for $\gamma$ lying both in $\Gamma_t$ and in $\Gamma_t(\ell)$ and $x,x'$ related by `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\iota_0(\gamma)$; `hetℓ`, the same unique-lifting property as `het` with $M_\ell$ in place of $M$; `hliftsurjℓ`, surjectivity on geometric points with prescribed $Onr$-component: for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is a $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra, every $\psi : Onr \to k$ and every $y \in M_\ell(k)$ there are $P \in \Omega(k)$ and $g \in G$ with $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g) = y$; and `hfibℓ`, the description of the fibres over such a $k$: $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g) = \Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi',P'),g')$ holds if and only if there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_t(\ell)$ such that $g' = \theta_t(\gamma)g$, $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and for every $y \in Onr$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\,v\det \iota_0(z)}$ for all scalar $z \in \Gamma_t$ (those with $z = c \cdot 1$ for some $c \in \mathbb Q$) with $\theta_t(z) = 1$, one has $\psi'(y) = \psi\bigl(\mathrm{Fr}^{-v\det \iota_0(\gamma)}(y)\bigr)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every scheme $T$ with $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and every family $\rho'$ assigning to each $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ a map $\mathcal F(B) \to T(B)$ which is natural in $B$ and satisfies the same twisted invariance as `hinvℓ` (for $\gamma$ in $\Gamma_t$ and in $\Gamma_t(\ell)$, and $x,x'$ related by `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\iota_0(\gamma)$, $\rho'(x',\theta_t(\gamma)g) = \rho'(x,g)$), there exists a family $u$ assigning to each $\pi$-nilpotent $B$ a map $M_\ell(B) \to T(B)$ such that:
--
--   1. $u$ is natural in $B$: for every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi : B \to B'$ between $\pi$-nilpotent algebras and every $y \in M_\ell(B)$, $u(M_\ell(\varphi)(y)) = T(\varphi)(u(y))$;
--
--   2. $u \circ \Theta_{f,\ell} = \rho'$ : for every $\pi$-nilpotent $B$ and every $x \in \mathcal F(B)$, $u(\Theta_{f,\ell}(x)) = \rho'(x)$;
--
--   3. $u$ is the only such family: any $u'$ assigning to each $\pi$-nilpotent $B$ a map $M_\ell(B) \to T(B)$ which is natural in $B$ and satisfies $u' \circ \Theta_{f,\ell} = \rho'$ agrees with $u$ on $M_\ell(B)$ for every $\pi$-nilpotent $B$.
--
--   This is the universal property — a categorical-quotient statement for the functor of $\pi$-nilpotent points — of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation family at one prime $\ell$ of the Hecke tower: the nilpotent-points functor of $M_\ell$ receives, from the $\Gamma_t \cap \Gamma_t(\ell)$-twisted-invariant families on $\bigl(\operatorname{Hom}(Onr,-) \times \Omega\bigr) \times G$, a unique factorisation through $\Theta_{f,\ell}$. It is used in the assembly of the uniformisation of the whole tower over the fine moduli scheme.
